[[File:Crafting tutor chathead.png|left]]
'''Cadmus''', the '''Crafting tutor''', is one of the several [[tutor]] guides stationed in [[Lumbridge]]. He provides different information about [[Crafting]] depending on one's Crafting level to both new and advanced players.

He can be found in a room on the {{FloorNumber|uk=1}} of the [[Lumbridge Castle]] containing a [[spinning wheel]].

==Dialogue==
{{Hastranscript|npc}}

{{Tutors}}
{{Lumbridge}}

{{Infobox Item |name = Craftsman scroll |image = [[File:Craftsman scroll.png]] |release = [[15 October]] [[2025]] |update = Grid Master - Out Today! |members = No |quest = No |tradeable = No |bankable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Read, Destroy |examine = Use this to select three Artisan skills to bond together, and share gained experience points. |value = 1 |weight = 0.010 |id = 31214 }} [[File:Craftsman scroll detail.png|130px|left]] '''Craftsman scroll''' is an item obtained after unlocking the [[Craftsman]] perk in the [[Grid Master]] community event. After subduing [[Tempoross]], the player is given the Craftsman benefit, which allows the following: * Select three artisan skills (from [[Construction]], [[Cooking]], [[Crafting]], [[Firemaking]], [[Fletching]], [[Herblore]], [[Runecraft]], and [[Smithing]]). * Whenever the player gains XP in one of those three skills, they will gain 50% of that XP in the other 2 selected skills as well.
The choices are permanent and the scroll is removed from the player once the picks have been made.
==Transcript== {{hastranscript|transclude=yes}}
{{Grid Master}}

{{External|rs|rsc}} {{Infobox Location |name = Crandor |image = [[File:Crandor.png]] |release = [[23 September]] [[2001]] |update = Dragon quest online! |members = No |location = [[Ardent Ocean]], [[Karamja]] |teleport = None |music = [[The Shadow]] |map = {{Map|name=Crandor|x=2836|y=3271|height=350|width=300|zoom=2}} |type = island |leagueRegion = Karamja }} {{Relativelocation |location = Crandor |north = Entrana |west = Fishing Platform |south = Karamja Volcano |east = Crafting Guild }} '''Crandor''' is a small volcanic island north of [[Karamja]]. Players are unable to [[Sailing|sail]] to Crandor themselves, but can buy the [[Lady Lumbridge|last remaining ship that can handle Crandor's reefs]] from [[Klarense]]. Players seek out this boat during [[Dragon Slayer I]], when the [[Guildmaster]] tasks them with defeating the mighty [[dragon]] [[Elvarg]].
==History== {{LoreSources|Dragon Slayer I|Melzar's notes|Klarense|Duke Horacio|Guildmaster|dialogue3=yes|dialogue4=yes|dialogue5=yes|the5=yes|{{RSL|Transcript:Postbag suffers from feature creep.|Postbag suffers from feature creep.}}}}
Crandor was once a thriving community, considered to be as politically important as [[Falador]] or [[Varrock]]. Crandorians were known for their ships, among other popular traded wares. Its size was much greater than the cove that remains today, as much of the city teetered on wharfs and piers that stretched out into the ocean. The island itself was the center of trade, with people from [[Asgarnia]], [[Misthalin]], the [[Fremennik Province]], [[Kandarin]], and [[Karamja]] all showing up to buy and sell. However, Crandorian traders eventually stopped coming to the mainland, due to an adventurer disturbing the dragon Elvarg, who lived under the volcano.
The adventurer perished, along with all but three survivors: a trio of wizards named [[Thalzar]], [[Lozar]] and [[Melzar the Mad|Melzar]], who split up the only surviving map back to Crandor as they couldn't bring themselves to destroy it. After reaching the mainland, the three survivors parted ways. Lozar built a [[Lozar's house|home in Lumbridge]], and Thalzar built a vault in the [[Dwarven Mine]]. Melzar settled in [[Rimmington]], where Crandorian survivors first fled, only for them to be tracked down by Elvarg and killed. Melzar sought to use necromancy to revive the survivors but was slowly driven to madness in the process; he never succeeded in reviving them, but he did reanimate the bones of many of the victims, and the [[Ghost (Melzar's Maze)|ghosts]] in his home have vague memories of the dragon attack.
The mainland was terrified that Elvarg would follow the wizards there and lay waste to all of Asgarnia and Misthalin, but thankfully, Elvarg returned to her cave under the volcano. Some time later, a brave adventurer found the pieces of the map, learned the path to Crandor, and ventured down into the volcano to vanquish the fearsome dragon. However, Elvarg did manage to score one final casualty, slaying [[Cabin Boy Jenkins|the cabin boy on the adventurer's ship]]. The cabin boy, Jenkins, later returned to the island as a ghost, and began [[Crew Management|offering his services]] to players looking for help while [[Sailing]].
==Transportation== [[File:Crandor and Karamja Dungeon wall.png|left|thumb|200x200px|Location of the false wall.]] Crandor is first be accessed by boat during the [[Dragon Slayer I]] [[quest]]. Players must obtain all three map pieces and repair the boat; after this, Ned will bring them to the island. After the quest, Crandor can only be accessed via a secret door in the [[Crandor and Karamja Dungeon]].
To reach the Crandor surface, players must first enter the Karamja Volcano, either by exiting the TzHaar City, or by climbing down from Karamja. The wall can be found in the north-east corner of the area. After passing the wall, players can run north, to the rope they placed during Dragon Slayer I, and climb up the rope to reach the surface. [[File:Elvarg.png|thumb|The fearsome dragon Elvarg.]]
==Locations== Crandor has multiple ores which players can mine through the [[Mining]] skill, labelled on the map with a small pickaxe. There are four [[Mining site|mining areas]] on the island, each guarded by their own monster. Due to the level of the monsters and their drops, it's a common island for mid-to-high level [[free-to-play]] players to train on, especially when [[Ranged|ranging]] from the many [[safespots]]. All of the monsters attack with [[melee]]. Players can encounter these monsters again in the dungeon below, as well as [[Deadly red spider|deadly red spiders]] and [[Elvarg]]. {| class="wikitable" !Location !Ores available !Level for non-aggression |- |South-west beach |7 [[mithril rocks]] |45 |- |North-east beach |3 [[gold rocks]] |65 |- |South foothill |3 [[coal rocks]], 3 [[adamantite rocks]] |85 |- |North foothill |7 coal rocks, 1 mithril rock |81 |}
=== Dungeon === Underneath the island is a dungeon which connects to [[Karamja]], labelled on the map with a red exclamation mark. Players can climb down the hole at the top of the island to enter. In it are more skeletons, [[lesser demon]]s, and Elvarg, as well as some [[giant bats]] and [[deadly red spiders]] on the Karamjan side.
Elvarg resides in her own section of the dungeon. To the north of her cave is a laboratory, accessed during [[Dragon Slayer II]].
== Inhabitants == The inhabitant is [[Cabin Boy Jenkins]], who returns to the island [[Cabin Boy Jenkins (ghost)|as a ghost]] after [[Dragon Slayer I]] is complete. Beyond him, the island has many monsters:
* [[Elvarg]] * [[King scorpion]] (x6) * [[Hobgoblin]] (x6) * [[Lesser demon]] (2 on the surface and 5 on the Crandor side of the dungeon) * [[Moss giant]] (x3) * [[Skeleton]] (9 on the surface and 14 on the Crandor side of the dungeon)
== Music == {| class="wikitable sortable" !Name ! class="unsortable" |Unlock details ! class="unsortable" |Music track |- |[[Attack 2]] |Unlocked in the [[Crandor and Karamja Dungeon]]. |[[File:Attack 2.ogg]] |- |[[The Shadow]] |Unlocked on Crandor's surface. |[[File:The Shadow.ogg]] |}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 8 May 2024 |update = Project Rebalance: Skilling & Poll 81 MTA Changes |change = A [[Rocks (Crandor)|Crandor Rock Climb shortcut]] from the isle's peak to its southern side was added, requiring level 84 Agility. }} {{Subject changes |date = 18 June 2007 |update = The Dragonfire Shield |change = Crandor was graphically updated in order to "make it look more like the woeful place it became after Elvarg arrived". }} {{Subject changes footer}}
==Trivia== *After completing [[Dragon Slayer I]] quest, [[Ned]] can be found on the broken ship on Crandor, but will not talk about the task for the [[Lumbridge & Draynor Diary]]. *Crandor is the only island to be fully accessed on [[free-to-play]]. **A few tiles on the western side of the island are not accessible on free-to-play worlds, as they formerly played the members' only track [[Fruits de Mer]]. Although Fruits de Mer was removed from Crandor in April 2021, the tiles still remain members-only. *Prior to an update on [[18 June]] [[2007]], Crandor was covered in lush foliage. *On the south-western part of the island, next to the [[mithril rocks]], there are three so-called [[Game_square#Types_of_tiles|'force-walk'-tiles]] that will force the player to another tile when stepped on.
{{Dragon Slayer I}}

