'''Crash Island Dungeon''' is a very small dungeon containing five level 84 poisonous [[big snake]]s. The [[pit (Crash Island)|entrance]] is found in the centre of [[Crash Island]].

The dungeon is visited during the [[Recipe for Disaster]] subquest [[Recipe for Disaster#Awowogei|Freeing King Awowogei]]. Upon entering the dungeon for the first time, 15 damage is suffered. A rope is already provided within the pit to descend into the dungeon; the same [[rope (Crash Island Dungeon)|rope]] can be used to exit the dungeon. Logging out or lobbying will also put the player outside the dungeon. A few level 9 [[snake]]s are found above ground near the entrance to the dungeon; both types of snake are not aggressive to higher levelled players.

If you are too close to the walls, the snakes popping in and out of holes can hurt and poison you as well. These snakes are unattackable. Snakes will also pop out of the floor and every single hole in the wall when you first enter the dungeon, but most of them will not pop out after.

==Recipe for Disaster==
During the subquest [[Recipe for Disaster#Awowogei|Freeing King Awowogei]], players must enter the pit, and kill one of the big snakes to get a [[snake corpse]]. Players then have to stuff the snake corpse with [[Tchiki nut paste]] and a [[sliced red banana]] which will yield a [[raw stuffed snake]]. Players may want to get more than one snake corpse, since it is possible to burn the raw stuffed snake.

{{Freeing King Awowogei}}
{{Dungeons}}

{{External|rs=Crashed star}} {{Infobox Scenery |defver = 9 |version1 = Size-1 |version2 = Size-2 |version3 = Size-3 |version4 = Size-4 |version5 = Size-5 |version6 = Size-6 |version7 = Size-7 |version8 = Size-8 |version9 = Size-9 |name = Crashed Star |image1 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 1).png|300px]] |image2 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 2).png|300px]] |image3 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 3).png|300px]] |image4 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 4).png|300px]] |image5 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 5).png|300px]] |image6 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 6).png|250px]] |image7 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 7).png|250px]] |image8 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 8).png|250px]] |image9 = [[File:Crashed Star (size 9).png|250px]] |release = [[17 March]] [[2021]] |update = Shooting Stars |members = No |quest = No |location = See [[Shooting Stars]] |options = Mine, Prospect |examine = This big rock has fallen from the sky. |map = No |id1 = 41229 |id2 = 41228 |id3 = 41227 |id4 = 41226 |id5 = 41225 |id6 = 41224 |id7 = 41223 |id8 = 41021 |id9 = 41020 |leagueRegion = No |dropversion = Varlamore }} '''Crashed stars''' are rocks that play a central role in the [[Shooting Stars]] [[Distraction and Diversion]]. They can be mined to obtain [[stardust]], which members can trade for rewards at [[Dusuri's Star Shop]]. The stars can also be mined on free-to-play (F2P) worlds, but only grant half the experience given on members' worlds and the stardust collected has no use for F2P players.
The size of a crashed star decreases by 1 every 7 minutes. The crashed star disappears completely when either a size-1 star has been mined for 7 minutes, when another star crashes on the same world, or when a system update occurs. The [[skilling success rate]] and experience gained for successfully mining stardust is the same across all sizes.
The first player to interact with a crashed star will be listed on the [[Shooting Star Noticeboard|notice board]] in the [[Observatory]] on that world. The first player will also receive a star discovery bonus that gives 300 extra stardust as the star is mined. The player does not get any XP for this extra 300 stardust. This mechanism also applies on free-to-play worlds where it serves no useful purpose unless the player intends to purchase a membership at a later date. Discovering another star will result in the bonus stardust count resetting back to 300, even if some bonus stardust from a previous star is left. Players can also see the number of stars they were the first to discover on the notice board.
The effects of [[mining enhancers]] like the [[Varrock armour]] or [[Celestial signet]] do not work on crashed stars to get double the stardust.
==Landing sites== {{Main|Shooting Stars#Landing sites}} Shooting stars can land in a wide variety of locations across [[Gielinor]]'s surface. The size of a star when it lands is random, between 6 and 9. The level requirement to mine a star depends on its size.
{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center" !Size !{{SCP|Mining}} Level !Crash chance |- |9 || 90 || 20% |- |8 || 80 || 25% |- |7 || 70 || 30% |- |6 || 60 || 25% |- |5 || 50 || {{NA}} |- |4 || 40 || {{NA}} |- |3 || 30 || {{NA}} |- |2 || 20 || {{NA}} |- |1 || 10 || {{NA}} |}
