'''Crashed gliders''' are [[sea charting]] objects found south of the [[Karamja shipyard]] and north of [[Ape Atoll]].

Upon charting the glider in the [[Kharidian Sea]], a game message appears stating {{mes|You note the position of the crashed glider in your charts. From what you can tell, the glider crashed because strapping gnomes to paper aeroplanes is a flawed method of long distance travel.}}

Meanwhile, charting the glider in the [[Kharazi Strait]] results in a game message stating {{mes|You note the position of the crashed glider in your charts. From what you can tell, the glider crashed because the pilot attempted vertical takeoff.}}

{{Sea charting}}

{{Cache}} {{Infobox Item |name = Crasher |image = [[File:Crasher (RuneScape 2 Beta).png]] |release = [[1 December]] [[2003]] |update = RuneScape 2 Beta is Here! |removal = January-March 2004 |removalupdate = |members = No |quest = None |tradeable = |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = |options = crash, Drop |examine = A ball from the game Gnomeball |value = 1 |weight = |id = hist }} [[File:Crasher (RuneScape 2 Beta) detail.png|left|100px]] The '''Crasher''' was an unobtainable item only present during the ''RuneScape 2'' beta. It had an identical appearance and examine information to the [[Gnomeball]].
Its name suggests that it could possibly have been used in order to crash the game, although it is unknown why Jagex moderators would feel it necessary to create an item with this purpose.
{{Unobtainable items}}

'''Crashing''' may refer to:
*An item plummeting in price, similar to a {{wp|stock market crash}}. *A player using a spot already in use by another player, sometimes coincides with [[griefing]]. *A problem with the ''Old School RuneScape'' [[game client]], such as [[lag]] or an unexpected [[server blackout]].
{{Disambig}}

