furs (Aldarin) detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Crate of furs (Ardougne) detail.png|left|150px]] |version3 = [[File:Crate of furs (Catherby) detail.png|left|150px]] |version4 = [[File:Crate of furs (Deepfin Point) detail.png|left|150px]] |version5 = [[File:Crate of furs (Land's End) detail.png|left|150px]] |version6 = [[File:Crate of furs (Lunar Isle) detail.png|left|150px]] |version7 = [[File:Crate of furs (Piscatoris) detail.png|left|150px]] |version8 = [[File:Crate of furs (Port Piscarilius) detail.png|left|150px]] |version9 = [[File:Crate of furs (Port Roberts) detail.png|left|150px]] |version10 = [[File:Crate of furs (Port Tyras) detail.png|left|150px]] |version11 = [[File:Crate of furs (Red Rock) detail.png|left|150px]] }} A '''crate of furs''' is an item that may be obtained from a [[ledger table]] after taking on a [[courier task]], which must then be delivered to the corresponding destination's port by boarding their [[boat]] and sailing to said destination. Players without a crewmate to navigate their boat must store the crate in the [[cargo hold]] before they can man the helm.
Multiple of a crate may be required to be delivered for a courier task, in which case players must board their boat multiple times to store the crates (as they can only carry one at a time) or have a [[crewmate]] assist them, who will automatically take a crate when the player does so. While any crewmate can carry a crate, those with Deckhandiness levels of at least 3 can carry two at once.
Players cannot unequip the crate normally, nor can they teleport or leave the port area with the crate equipped. If the player leaves the area, a game message appears stating {{mes|You're leaving port with some cargo. If you do not return it, it will be confiscated by the shipwright wizard's autonomous tracking unit.|colour=#ff3045}} After 22 ticks (13.2s), the crate will be removed with an accompanying game message stating {{mes|Your cargo has been confiscated by the S.W.A.T. team.|colour=#ff0000}}
