{{Infobox Item |version1 = Deepfin Point |version2 = Etceteria |version3 = Port Khazard |version4 = Port Piscarilius |version5 = Rellekka |version6 = Ruins of Unkah |name = Crate of planks |image1 = [[File:Crate of planks (Deepfin Point).png]] |image2 = [[File:Crate of planks (Etceteria).png]] |image3 = [[File:Crate of planks (Port Khazard).png]] |image4 = [[File:Crate of planks (Port Piscarilius).png]] |image5 = [[File:Crate of planks (Rellekka).png]] |image6 = [[File:Crate of planks (Ruins of Unkah).png]] |release = [[19 November]] [[2025]] |update = Sailing is OUT TODAY! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine1 = A cargo crate of planks destined for Deepfin Point. |examine2 = A cargo crate of planks destined for Etceteria. |examine3 = A cargo crate of planks destined for Port Khazard. |examine4 = A cargo crate of planks destined for Port Piscarilius. |examine5 = A cargo crate of planks destined for Rellekka. |examine6 = A cargo crate of planks destined for the Ruins of Unkah. |value = 0 |alchable = No |weight = 1.285 |id1 = 32544,32950,32953,32955,32957 |id2 = 32556 |id3 = 32624 |id4 = 32645,32966,32971 |id5 = 32743,32992 |id6 = 32755 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Crate of planks (Deepfin Point) detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Crate of planks (Etceteria) detail.png|left|150px]] |version3 = [[File:Crate of planks (Port Khazard) detail.png|left|150px]] |version4 = [[File:Crate of planks (Port Piscarilius) detail.png|left|150px]] |version5 = [[File:Crate of planks (Rellekka) detail.png|left|150px]] |version6 = [[File:Crate of planks (Ruins of Unkah) detail.png|left|150px]] }} A '''crate of planks''' is an item that may be obtained from a [[ledger table]] after taking on a [[courier task]], which must then be delivered to the corresponding destination's port by boarding their [[boat]] and sailing to said destination. Players without a crewmate to navigate their boat must store the crate in the [[cargo hold]] before they can man the helm.
Multiple of a crate may be required to be delivered for a courier task, in which case players must board their boat multiple times to store the crates (as they can only carry one at a time) or have a [[crewmate]] assist them, who will automatically take a crate when the player does so. While any crewmate can carry a crate, those with Deckhandiness levels of at least 3 can carry two at once.
Players cannot unequip the crate normally, nor can they teleport or leave the port area with the crate equipped. If the player leaves the area, a game message appears stating {{mes|You're leaving port with some cargo. If you do not return it, it will be confiscated by the shipwright wizard's autonomous tracking unit.|colour=#ff3045}} After 22 ticks (13.2s), the crate will be removed with an accompanying game message stating {{mes|Your cargo has been confiscated by the S.W.A.T. team.|colour=#ff0000}}
