{{Otheruses|def=no|his bow|Craw's bow}} [[File:Craw's bow detail.png|right|150px|thumb|[[Craw's bow]], the only memento of one of [[Armadyl]]'s most formidable followers.]] '''Craw''' was a follower of [[Armadyl]] and fought for him during the [[God Wars]]. They have been described as a formidable archer who personally eliminated some of Armadyl's greatest enemies.
When the God Wars ended, Craw was one of the many soldiers killed in the destruction of [[Forinthry]]. Now, an undead Craw can be found amongst the [[revenants]] of the [[Wilderness]], still wielding the [[Craw's bow|trusted bow]] that helped them in the past.{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/revenant-cave-rewards-revisited-content-poll--theatre-of-blood?oldschool=1|title=Revenant Cave Rewards: Revisited, Content Poll & Theatre of Blood|newsdate=27 June 2018|quote=Of all of Armadyl's followers in the God Wars, few were more formidable than Craw. An expert with the bow, Craw personally eliminated some of Armadyl's greatest enemies. When the God Wars ended, Craw was one of the many soldiers killed in the destruction of Forinthry. Now, an undead Craw can be found amongst the revenants of the Wilderness, still wielding the trusted bow that helped them in the past.}}
It is unknown whether or not Craw was an [[aviansie]] like most Armadyleans or a different species entirely, as aviansie cannot be found within the Revenant Caves, the only location where the revenants reside.
==References== {{Reflist}}
[[Category:Armadyleans]] [[Category:Characters from the Third Age]] [[Category:Characters that do not appear in-game]] [[Category:Deceased characters]]

{{Redirect|C bow|another bow shortened similarly|crystal bow}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Uncharged |version2 = Charged |name1 = Craw's bow (u) |name2 = Craw's bow |image1 = [[File:Craw's bow (u).png]] |image2 = [[File:Craw's bow.png]] |release = [[26 July]] [[2018]] |update = Revenant Cave Rewards and Troll Quest Announcement |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = Yes |tradeable2 = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable1 = Yes |noteable2 = No |options1 = Wield, Dismantle, Drop |options2 = Wield, Check, Uncharge |wornoptions1 = None |wornoptions2 = Check |destroy1 = None |destroy2 = Uncharge - ''If you uncharge this weapon, all the revenant ether will return to your inventory.'' |examine = This bow once belonged to a formidable follower of Armadyl. |value = 120000 |weight = 3.175 |exchange1 = Yes |exchange2 = No |id1 = 22547 |id2 = 22550 |leagueRegion = Wilderness }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Craw's bow (u) detail.png|left|180px]] |version2 = [[File:Craw's bow detail.png|left|180px]] }} [[File:Craw's bow attack.png|thumb|275px|A player attacks a target with Craw's bow.]] '''Craw's bow''' is a [[shortbow (weapon)|shortbow]] once owned by [[Craw]], one of the more formidable followers among [[Armadyl]]'s forces during the [[God Wars]]. It can be received as a drop from [[revenants]] found within the [[Revenant Caves]]. This item counts as an [[Armadyl]] item in the [[God Wars Dungeon]].
The bow requires a [[Ranged]] level of 60 to wield, and shares the same bonuses as the [[magic shortbow (i)]] with the ranged strength of [[dragon arrow]]s, although it does not have a [[special attack]]. It has to be charged with [[revenant ether]] to be fired, but it does provide its own ammo, rolling damage against an NPC's standard ranged defence. It also has a powerful [[passive effect]] within the [[Wilderness]].
The bow's fired shots are coated in a yellow-orange aura, similar to the crystal bow. The bow has an [[attack range]] of 9. Longrange increases attack range by 1.
The bow can be upgraded to a [[webweaver bow]] by attaching the [[fangs of Venenatis]] to it, requiring level 85 Fletching or paying [[Derse Venator]] 500,000 coins. Players can also dismantle an uncharged bow to receive 7,500 [[revenant ether]], resulting in a loss of {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|7500}}-{{GEP|Craw's bow (u)}}|c}}.
==Combat stats== {{Infobox Bonuses |version1 = Uncharged |version2 = Charged |astab = 0 |aslash = 0 |acrush = 0 |amagic = 0 |arange = +75 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |drange = 0 |str = 0 |rstr = +60 |mdmg = 0 |prayer = 0 |slot = 2h |speed = 4 |attackrange = 9 |combatstyle = Bow |image1 = [[File:Craw's bow (u) equipped.png|170px]] |image2 = [[File:Craw's bow equipped.png|170px]] |altimage1 = [[File:Craw's bow (u) equipped female.png|170px]] |altimage2 = [[File:Craw's bow equipped female.png|170px]] }}
{{CombatStyles|Bow|speed=4|attackrange=9}}
==Passive effect== When Craw's bow is charged with [[revenant ether]], an additional 50% ranged accuracy and damage boost is applied when attacking any [[NPC]] in the [[Wilderness]], consuming 1 ether per attack whether the player hits or not.
This effect will stack additively with a [[Slayer helmet (i)]] or multiplicatively with a [[Salve amulet(i)]] and their variants, but not both simultaneously. This makes it the second strongest ranged weapon in the Wilderness after the [[webweaver bow]], surpassing the damage output of a [[toxic blowpipe]] with [[dragon dart]]s.
==Charging and death== To use the bow, it must first be activated with 1,000 [[revenant ether]] (costing {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|1000}}|c}}). Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. The 1,000 ether used to activate the bow '''does not''' count towards the ammo usage of the bow, thus additional ether must be added (up to 16,000) to fire it. Using the bow requires revenant ether whether inside the wilderness or not, but the 50% ranged accuracy and damage boost only applies while inside the wilderness.
The Craw's bow uses 1 [[revenant ether]] per shot and fires 2,000 shots per hour on the rapid attack style. Thus the hourly cost of constantly using this weapon is 2,000 ether or {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|2000}}|c}} on Rapid, or 1,500 ether or {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|1500}}|c}} on Accurate/Longrange.
The ether can be safely removed by selecting the right-click ''Uncharge'' option on the bow, after which, the bow becomes tradeable again.
Upon [[death]] within the Wilderness, any revenant ether stored as ammo within the bow will '''always''' be dropped and the initial 1,000 activation ether will '''always''' disappear, even if it is one of the player's protected items. Therefore, dying with an activated bow incurs a minimum loss of 1,000 ether. Despite the bow being able to store a maximum of 17,000 revenant ether, it is recommended to store the minimum amount required for a trip into the Wilderness (in addition to the 1,000 ether required to activate the weapon).
