{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Teak display |version2 = Mahogany display |version3 = Gilded display |name = Crawling hand |image1 = [[File:Crawling hand (mounted) built.png|220px]] |image2 = [[File:Crawling hand (mahogany display) built.png|220px]] |image3 = [[File:Crawling hand (gilded display) built.png|220px]] |release1 = [[31 May]] [[2006]] |release2 = [[27 February]] [[2025]] |release3 = [[27 February]] [[2025]] |update1 = PLAYER-OWNED HOUSES! |update2 = Game Jam: POH Improvements |update3 = Game Jam: POH Improvements |members = Yes |quest = No |location = [[Player-owned house]] [[skill hall]] |options1 = Talk-to, Trophies, Upgrade, Remove |options2 = Talk-to, Trophies, Upgrade, Remove |options3 = Talk-to, Trophies, Remove |examine = A trophy of a mighty slayer! |map = No |id1 = 56113 |id2 = 56114 |id3 = 56115 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Crawling hand (mounted) chathead.png|left]] |version2 = [[File:Crawling hand (mahogany display) chathead.png|left]] |version3 = [[File:Crawling hand (gilded display) chathead.png|left]] }} A mounted '''crawling hand''' is a basic trophy made by adding a [[stuffed crawling hand]] to either a [[Teak display (head trophy)|teak]], [[Mahogany display (head trophy)|mahogany]], or [[gilded display]] within the [[skill hall]] in a [[player-owned house]]. When added to a display (which requires being in building mode), the player is given 31 [[Construction]] and 261 [[Slayer]] [[experience]].
Mounted trophies are saved per [[account]], and are shared between all other trophy displays in a house. Duplicate hands can be added for additional experience, provided that the player has stuffed them and are in building mode; however they '''cannot''' be removed to retrieve the stuffed hand.
As stuffing services are exclusive to the [[Taxidermist]] in [[Canifis]], mounting trophies require completion of [[Priest in Peril]].
