{{external|rsc=A Silver Dagger|rs}}{{otheruses|the item used during the [[Murder Mystery]] [[quest]]|the item used during the [[Misthalin Mystery]] [[quest]]|Killer's knife}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Normal |version2 = Dusted |name = Criminal's dagger |image = [[File:Criminal's dagger.png]] |release = [[9 June]] [[2003]] |update = New Murder Mystery Quest! |members = Yes |quest = [[Murder Mystery]] |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine1 = A flimsy-looking dagger found at the crime scene. |examine2 = A flimsy-looking dagger found at the crime scene coated with a thin layer of flour. |value = 1 |weight = 0.453 |respawn = 100 |id1 = 1813 |id2 = 1814 }} [[File:Criminal's dagger detail.png|left|110px]] The '''Criminal's dagger''' is a quest [[item]] that is found at the murder scene during the [[Murder Mystery]] [[quest]]. This dagger cannot be equipped and is used to help gather evidence against the culprit during the quest. In the quest, you must use a [[pot of flour]] on the dagger to dust it, then use [[flypaper]] on the dagger to get the [[unknown print]]. You must do the same with the items belonging to the suspects. Then compare them by using a suspect's fingerprints on the criminal's fingerprint to get the [[killer's print]].
If you lose it, it will [[respawn]] in the same place as where you got it.
