{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Monster |name = Crypt rat |image = [[File:Crypt rat.png|280px]] |release = [[9 May]] [[2005]] |update = Barrows |members = Yes |combat = 43 |size = 1 |examine = A nasty little rodent. |attributes = rat |xpbonus = 0 |max hit = 3 |aggressive = Yes |poisonous = No |attack style = [[Stab]] |attack speed = 4 |respawn = 50 |slayxp = 35 |cat = Rats |assignedby = turael,spria |hitpoints = 35 |att = 70 |str = 20 |def = 20 |mage = 1 |range = 1 |attbns = 0 |strbns = 0 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |dlight = 0 |dstandard = 0 |dheavy = 0 |poisonresistance = 0 |venomresistance = 0 |immunecannon = No |immunethrall = No |id = 1679 }} '''Crypt rats''' are [[rat]]s lurking in the [[Barrows]] tunnels. Crypt rats are one of the many obstacles between a player and the chest containing rewards where they constantly distract players from completing puzzles. As with all monsters in the crypts, they are [[aggressiveness|aggressive]] to any player regardless of their [[combat level]]. They may [[spawn]] whenever the player opens a door in the tunnels.
Players can command their [[cat]]s to attempt to catch the crypt rat, but cats of all types will refuse to go after it, with varying dialogue depending on the cat type. [[Wily cat]]s will even damage the player for 3 hitpoints if they try to make it catch a crypt rat, which is capable of being lethal if the player is at 3 hitpoints or lower.
Killing a crypt rat will increase the player's rewards potential by 43 (4.25%).
