==Crystal equipment==
{{Main|Crystal equipment}}
Weapons and armour start with a charge of 2,500 losing one charge every time it is used. When the item completely degrades it will revert to a crystal seed. Items cannot be charged or traded until they are in this seed form. They are also tradeable immediately after recharging.

Tools degrade differently and do not revert to the tool seed form when depleted. Instead of reverting, the tool will become unusable until the player charges them with more crystal shards.

The following items are made of elven crystal:
{{:Crystal singing}}
[[Category:Elves]]

[[File:Crystal-flecked waters.png|thumb|The crystal-flecked pool]]
'''Crystal-flecked''' waters are a [[Sailing hazards|sailing hazard]] that are found in the waters near [[Tirannwn]], such as in [[Porth Gwenith]] and [[Porth Neigwl]]. Unprepared boats that attempt to traverse these waters without an [[adamant keel]] or better will be slowed and rapidly dealt 20 damage. [[Raft]]s cannot be upgraded to resist this effect, as they do not have a [[keel]].

These waters are the remains of a naval battle that took place during the [[Siege of Prifddinas]], where hundreds of crystal elven vessels were destroyed and scattered in the ocean. 

