==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 12 March 2025 |update = Permanent Deadman: World 345 Improvements |change = The [[crystal halberd]], crystal bow, and [[crystal shield]] supports a bank item option for changing charges, with all three items sharing the same "Quantity" value, using Crystal charges instead of coins. }} {{Subject changes |date = 30 June 2021 |update = Phosani's Nightmare |poll = Equipment Rebalance: Ranged Meta |change = The bow's [[Ranged Strength]] bonus has been increased from +70 to +78. }} {{Subject changes |date = 25 July 2019 |update = Song of the Elves |poll = Song of the Elves rewards |change = Crystal equipment stats no longer become gradually lower as the weapon degrades, converting all imbued crystal bows into crystal weapon seeds and removing the ability to imbue them through [[Nightmare Zone]]. The crystal bow can now alternatively be made through crystal shards instead of paying Ilfeen. }} {{Subject changes |date = 16 April 2015 |update = Clan Wars Game Modes & More |change = A "Check" option was added to see the remaining charges. }} {{Subject changes |date = 13 March 2014 |update = Rejuvenating the Wilderness: More risk, more reward |change = Crystal equipment now reverts to a seed when dropped on death. }} {{Subject changes |date = 26 September 2013 |update = Patch Notes (26 September 2013) |poll = Old School feature poll 10: New Rewards |change = Crystal bows and shields can be imbued, making them keep their combat stats unchanged as they degrade. }} {{Subject changes |date = 9 May 2005 |update = Barrows |change = The bow's [[attack speed]] was increased from 6 to 5. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
==Trivia== *Attempting to cast [[Low Level Alchemy]] or [[High Level Alchemy]] on a crystal bow results in the message ''"You can't do that to elven crystal!"'' This is due to a [[glitch]] that allowed players to alchemise crystal bows on [[free-to-play]] worlds for {{NoCoins|540,000|c}} each. Players could buy crystal seeds, enchant them into bows for {{NoCoins|180,000|c}}, and alchemise the bows for significant profit. Because of this, Jagex made it impossible to alchemise members' objects on free-to-play worlds, and made it impossible to alchemise crystal equipment. *The crystal bow requires 50 Agility to equip, however it is impossible to navigate the forests of [[Tirannwn]] during the required quests without level 56 Agility (or as low as 51 with a [[summer pie]] boost).
