==Degrading== The crystal halberd degraded over time. After 250 hits, it degraded into a "'''Crystal halberd 9/10'''", and thereafter for every 250 hits, it would degrade another 1/10th, until it reverted into a [[crystal seed]] after a total of 2,500 hits, and had to be recharged before it could be used again. If the special attack was used and it hit an opponent twice or multiple opponents, it would be considered one hit in regards to degradation. As the halberd degraded, the negative [[Magic]] attack bonus remained the same while the positive attack bonuses decreased as shown below. {{Infotable Bonuses header}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd full |astab = +85 |aslash = +110 |acrush = +5 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +4 |dcrush = +5 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +118 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 9/10 |astab = +82 |aslash = +106 |acrush = +5 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +4 |dcrush = +5 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +113 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 8/10 |astab = +79 |aslash = +102 |acrush = +5 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +4 |dcrush = +5 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +108 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 7/10 |astab = +76 |aslash = +98 |acrush = +4 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +3 |dcrush = +4 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +103 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 6/10 |astab = +73 |aslash = +94 |acrush = +4 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +3 |dcrush = +4 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +98 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 5/10 |astab = +70 |aslash = +90 |acrush = +4 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +3 |dcrush = +4 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +93 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 4/10 |astab = +67 |aslash = +86 |acrush = +3 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +2 |dcrush = +3 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +88 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 3/10 |astab = +64 |aslash = +82 |acrush = +3 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +2 |dcrush = +3 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +83 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 2/10 |astab = +61 |aslash = +78 |acrush = +3 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +2 |dcrush = +3 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +78 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses row |name = Crystal halberd 1/10 |astab = +58 |aslash = +74 |acrush = +2 |amagic = -4 |arange = +0 |dstab = -1 |dslash = +1 |dcrush = +2 |dmagic = +0 |drange = +0 |str = +73 |rstr = +0 |mdmg = +0 |prayer = +0}} {{Infotable Bonuses footer}}
The crystal halberd could be imbued for 2,000 [[Nightmare Zone]] points per charge to create a [[crystal halberd (i)]], requiring 20,000 points to imbue a fully charged halberd. Imbuing the crystal halberd did not keep it from degrading, however its stats would remain at their maximum, regardless of how much it had degraded. When the halberd reverted back to a crystal seed, it would lose its imbue, and players had to imbue it again using points from the Nightmare Zone. Additionally, imbuing a crystal halberd that had already degraded to 9/10 or below would restore the halberd's stats to their maximum.
==Recharging== [[Ilfeen]] recharged [[crystal seed]]s into [[crystal bow]]s, [[crystal shield]]s ''or'' crystal halberds. Initially, Ilfeen charged 750,000 coins to re-enchant a crystal seed into a crystal halberd. However, the price decreased by 150,000 coins each time Ilfeen re-enchanted a seed for a player, in the following manner, until reaching the minimum recharge cost of 150,000 coins:
{| class="wikitable" !Enchantment !Cost for re-enchantment |- |First |750,000 |- |Second |600,000 |- |Third |450,000 |- |Fourth |300,000 |- |Fifth and thereafter |150,000 |}
The amount that Ilfeen charges is dependent on the number of crystal seeds she has re-enchanted, '''not''' the number of crystal halberds she has recharged. For example, a player who pays Ilfeen 900,000 coins to re-enchant a crystal seed into a crystal bow will only have to pay her 600,000 coins to recharge a seed into a crystal halberd.
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 25 July 2019 |update = Song of the Elves |change = *All variants of the halberd had their values decreased to 1. *The "Wield" option was replaced by a fake Wield option. *The item was made usable by free to play players, but it is now unobtainable. *The item could no longer be turned into a bank placeholder. }} {{Subject changes |date = 23 May 2019 |update = Hosidius Rework and Deadman Beta |change = The offensive and defensive stats of the unimbued crystal halberd now correctly lower as the weapon degrades. }} {{Subject changes |date = 26 April 2019 |type = hotfix |change = The crystal halberd special attack was limited to three targets in PVP, to prevent unintentionally high [[experience]] rates.{{CiteTwitter|url=https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/1121800161104019457|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/101623|archivedate=28 August 2021|author=Old School RuneScape|date=26 April 2019|quote=A hotfix has been deployed to cap the Crystal halberd, Crystal halberd (i), Dragon halberd, and Dragon two handed sword special attacks to hit a maximum of 3 players in PvP. This is to prevent players achieving unintentionally high xp rates while a long term fix is discussed.}} }} {{Subject changes |date = 7 June 2018 |update = The Theatre of Blood |change = The crystal halberd's special attack used to only hit the main target on the central tile, but hit an unlimited amount of monsters on the two adjacent tiles. Now, it caps the maximum number of monsters to 10, but allows monsters standing on the same tile as the primary target to also be affected by the attack. }} {{Subject changes |date = 19 May 2016 |update = Sand Crabs & Soul Bearers |change = The "uncharge" option on the crystal halberd now properly removes the weapon's imbue. Previously, it would result in the message "Nothing interesting happens". }} {{Subject changes |date = 25 June 2015 |update = Boss Room Counters & Platinum Tokens |change = The crystal halberd now becomes cheaper when re-enchanted. }} {{Subject changes |date = 23 April 2015 |update = Crystal Halberd Special & More |poll = Old School Content Poll 32: Resizable Mode |change = A special attack was added. }} {{Subject changes |date = 16 April 2015 |update = Clan Wars Game Modes & More |change = A "Check" option was added to see the remaining number of charges. }} {{Subject changes |date = 12 March 2015 |update = Diary Skillcape Emote |change = *The combat interface no longer shows unarmed option for the crystal halberd. *Attacking an opponent no longer shows the message "Unrecognised ranged weapon". *The "Uncharge" option was removed. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
