{{Otheruses|def=no|the version used in [[The Gauntlet]]|Crystal harpoon (The Gauntlet)}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Active |version2 = Inactive |name1 = Crystal harpoon |name2 = Crystal harpoon (inactive) |image1 = [[File:Crystal harpoon.png]] |image2 = [[File:Crystal harpoon (inactive).png]] |release = [[25 July]] [[2019]] |update = Song of the Elves |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Wield, Check, Revert, Drop |options2 = Wield, Revert, Drop |wornoptions1 = Check |wornoptions2 = None |examine = A very powerful harpoon. |value = 520000 |weight = 0.907 |id1 = 23762 |id2 = 23764 |leagueRegion = Desert&Tirannwn,Kourend&Tirannwn }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Crystal harpoon detail.png|left|130px]] |version2 = [[File:Crystal harpoon (inactive) detail.png|left|130px]] }} The '''crystal harpoon''' is an untradeable [[harpoon]] created via [[crystal singing]] after finishing [[Song of the Elves]]. It requires 71 [[Fishing]], 70 [[Attack]], and 50 [[Agility]] to wield and degrades during use like other [[crystal equipment]]. It can be stored in a [[tackle box]].
While fishing, the charged harpoon provides a 35% increased catch rate over the regular harpoon ''(a 12.5% increase compared with the [[dragon harpoon]])'', the highest for all harpoons. This effect only works on fish that utilise the harpoon (sharks etc). Whilst fighting [[Tempoross]], an additional effect transforms 1/3 of caught fish into [[Crystallised harpoonfish]], which grant 20% more fishing experience when used as ammunition. The crystal harpoon only provides a 10% increased catch chance at Tempoross, rather than 35%.
Players can create a crystal harpoon via a [[singing bowl]] by combining a dragon harpoon, 120 [[crystal shard]]s and a [[crystal tool seed]]. Singing the crystal requires 76 [[Smithing]] and 76 [[Crafting]], which can be [[boosted]], and grants 6,000 experience in both skills. Players may bypass the skill requirements by having [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for an additional 60 crystal shards, bringing the total to 180.
The harpoon is created with 10,000 charges and a charge is consumed for every fish caught. Crystal shards can be used to recharge the harpoon, each providing 100 charges up to a maximum of 20,000. Players can configure the charges while the harpoon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials.
A dangerous death in PvP causes the crystal harpoon to revert to a dragon harpoon, which will then be dropped for the killer. All crystal shards will be lost should this happen.
==Combat stats== {{Infobox Bonuses |version1 = Active |version2 = Inactive |astab = +38 |aslash = +32 |acrush = 0 |amagic = 0 |arange = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = +1 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |drange = 0 |str = 42 |rstr = 0 |mdmg = 0 |prayer = 0 |slot = weapon |speed = 5 |attackrange = 1 |combatstyle = Stab Sword |image1 = [[File:Crystal harpoon equipped.png|230px]] |image2 = [[File:Crystal harpoon (inactive) equipped.png|230px]] |altimage = [[File:Crystal harpoon equipped female.png|230px]] }}
{{CombatStyles|Stab Sword|speed=5|attackrange=1}}
==Special attack== [[File:Fishstabber (crystal harpoon).gif|frame|A player performs the crystal harpoon's special attack, ''Fishstabber''.]] The crystal harpoon has the same [[special attacks|special attack]] as a [[dragon harpoon]], ''Fishstabber'', that provides a visible +3 [[boost]] to [[Fishing]], consuming 100% special attack energy. It cannot be used without the level 70 [[Attack]] and 50 [[Agility]] requirement to wield the harpoon.
Also note that any levels boosted above 99 with the special attack will be treated as 99. Therefore, you will start to receive diminishing returns with the special attack at level 97 and 98, with there being no value in activating the special attack at level 99.
==Creation== {{#vardefine:crystalshardvalue|{{#ifexpr:{{#vardefineecho:seedvalue|{{GEP|Enhanced crystal teleport seed}} / 150}} > {{#vardefineecho:divinesupercombatvalue|({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}} - {{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}}) / 0.4}} | {{#var:seedvalue}} | {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}}}} round 1}} {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 76 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 6,000 |skill2 = Crafting |skill2lvl = 76 |skill2boostable = Yes |skill2exp = 6,000 |members = Yes |ticks = 3 |ticksnote = Takes 3 ticks to create an entire inventory |facilities = Singing bowl |mat1 = Dragon harpoon |mat2 = Crystal tool seed |mat3 = Crystal shard |mat3quantity = 120 |mat3cost = {{#var:crystalshardvalue}} |mat3itemnote = Value based on {{#ifexpr:{{#var:seedvalue}} > {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}} | the cost of obtaining by exchanging [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s with [[Amrod]] | the potential profit of using the crystal shards to create [[divine super combat potion]]s}} |output1 = Crystal harpoon |output1cost = No }}
==Gaining and Consuming Charges== When created the crystal harpoon starts with 10,000 charges. Like all [[crystal equipment]] one charge is consumed for each successful use of the tool, in this case when a fish is caught or in Tempoross when harpooning the Spirit Pool. Once the harpoon's charges have been fully depleted, it can still be used for fishing and acts like a normal dragon harpoon.
Wearing an [[elven signet]] while using crystal equipment will provide a 10% chance to not consume charges.
Crystal shards can be used on the harpoon at any time to add 100 charges per shard, up to a maximum of 20,000. {| class="wikitable" {{#vardefine:charge_crystalshardvalue|{{#ifexpr:{{#vardefineecho:charge_seedvalue|({{GEP|Enhanced crystal teleport seed}} / 150) / 100}} > {{#vardefineecho:charge_divinesupercombatvalue|(({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}} - {{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}}) / 0.4) / 100}} | {{#var:charge_seedvalue}} | {{#var:charge_divinesupercombatvalue}}}} round 1}} {{#vardefine:signet_charge_crystalshardvalue|({{#var:charge_crystalshardvalue}}) * 0.8889 }} !Item !Cost per charge |- |{{plink|Crystal shard}} | {{Coins|({{#var:charge_crystalshardvalue}})}} {{efn|Value based on {{#ifexpr:{{#var:charge_seedvalue}} > {{#var:charge_divinesupercombatvalue}} | the cost of obtaining by exchanging [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s with [[Amrod]] | the potential profit of using the crystal shards to create [[divine super combat potion]]s}}|name=estimate}} |- |- |{{plinkp|Elven signet}} + {{plinkp|Crystal shard}} | {{Coins|({{#var:signet_charge_crystalshardvalue}})}} {{efn|name=estimate}}{{efn|Initial charges cost full amount, discount expressed as savings while wearing the [[Elven signet]]|name=signet}} |- |} {{notelist}}
===Disassembly=== The right-click option, ''Revert'', can be used at any time, returning the dragon harpoon and crystal tool seed used to make it. However, all crystal shards used to craft or charge the tool will be lost in the process.
