{{External|rs}} {{otheruses|the crystal helm}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Active |version2 = Inactive |name1 = Crystal helm |name2 = Crystal helm (inactive) |image1 = [[File:Crystal helm.png]] |image2 = [[File:Crystal helm (inactive).png]] |release = [[25 July]] [[2019]] |update = Song of the Elves |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Wear, Check, Revert, Drop |options2 = Wear, Revert, Drop |wornoptions1 = Check |wornoptions2 = None |examine = This helmet shines bright, like a diamond. |value = 500000 |alchable = No |weight = 0.500 |id1 = 23971 |id2 = 23973 |leagueRegion = Tirannwn }} {{Synced switch |version1=[[File:Crystal helm detail.png|left|110px]] [[File:Crystal helm chathead.png|left]] |version2=[[File:Crystal helm (inactive) detail.png|left|110px]] [[File:Crystal helm (inactive) chathead.png|left]] }} A '''crystal helm''' is a piece of [[crystal armour]] requiring level 70 [[Defence]] and 50 [[Agility]] to equip. When equipped, a 2.5% damage bonus and 5% accuracy bonus is applied when using the [[crystal bow]] or [[Bow of Faerdhinen]]. This bonus stacks additively with the [[crystal legs]] and [[crystal body]]'s bonuses, for a total of 15% damage and 30% accuracy.
Players can create a crystal helm via a [[singing bowl]] by combining 50 [[crystal shard]]s and a [[crystal armour seed]]. Doing so requires level 70 [[Smithing]] and [[Crafting]] to [[crystal singing|sing]] the crystal (the levels can be [[Temporary skill boost|boosted]]), and grants 2,500 experience in both skills. Players can configure the charges while the helm is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. If the player does not meet the Smithing and Crafting requirements, they can have [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for them for an extra 60 crystal shards, for a total of 110.
The helm's colours may also be changed to other colours of the [[Elven Clans]] by buying crystals from [[Lliann's Wares]] in [[Prifddinas]], which cost 500,000 coins each. It can also be reverted to its original colour by using the [[crystal of Meilyr]] on any variant of the helm.
If lost to another player in a dangerous PVP death, the crystal helm will revert to a crystal armour seed, which will then be dropped for the killer. All crystal shards will be lost should this happen. If the crystal helm is protected on death, the helmet will be kept, and will not lose any charges- similar to a blowpipe or trident.
==Combat stats== {{Infobox Bonuses |version1 = Active |version2 = Inactive |astab = 0 |aslash = 0 |acrush = 0 |amagic1 = -10 |amagic2 = 0 |arange1 = +9 |arange2 = 0 |dstab1 = +12 |dstab2 = 0 |dslash1 = +8 |dslash2 = 0 |dcrush1 = +14 |dcrush2 = 0 |dmagic1 = +10 |dmagic2 = 0 |drange1 = +18 |drange2 = 0 |str = 0 |rstr = 0 |mdmg = 0 |prayer1 = +2 |prayer2 = 0 |slot = head |image1 = [[File:Crystal helm equipped male.png|125px]] |image2 = [[File:Crystal helm (inactive) equipped male.png|125px]] |altimage1 = [[File:Crystal helm equipped female.png|125px]] |altimage2 = [[File:Crystal helm (inactive) equipped female.png|125px]] }}
==Creation== ===Armour seed=== {{#vardefine:crystalshardvalue|{{#ifexpr:{{#vardefineecho:seedvalue|{{GEP|Enhanced crystal teleport seed}} / 150}} > {{#vardefineecho:divinesupercombatvalue|({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}} - {{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}}) / 0.4}} | {{#var:seedvalue}} | {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}}}}}} {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 70 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 2,500 |skill2 = Crafting |skill2lvl = 70 |skill2boostable = Yes |skill2exp = 2,500 |members = Yes |ticks = 5 |ticksnote = Takes 5 ticks to create an entire inventory |facilities = Singing bowl |mat1 = Crystal armour seed |mat2 = Crystal shard |mat2quantity = 50 |mat2cost = {{#var:crystalshardvalue}} |mat2itemnote = Value based on {{#ifexpr:{{#var:seedvalue}} > {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}} | the cost of obtaining by exchanging [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s with [[Amrod]] | the potential profit of using the crystal shards to create [[divine super combat potion]]s}} |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No |output1subtxt = Creation }}
===Recolour=== {{Tabber |tab1 = Amlodd |tab1content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Amlodd) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab2 = Cadarn |tab2content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Cadarn) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab3 = Crwys |tab3content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Crwys) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab4 = Hefin |tab4content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Hefin) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab5 = Iorwerth |tab5content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Iorwerth) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab6 = Ithell |tab6content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Ithell) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} |tab7 = Trahaearn |tab7content = {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Crystal helm (Trahaearn) |mat1cost = No |mat2 = Crystal of meilyr |mat2cost = 500,000 |output1 = Crystal helm |output1cost = No }} }}
==Degradation== When created, the crystal helm starts off at 2,500 charges and degrades like all [[crystal equipment]], with one charge being depleted for each successful hit that is received from combat; once the helm's charges have been fully depleted, it will no longer have its set effect and stat bonuses until more charges are added to it. The damage from poison or venom will not deplete charges. Wearing an [[elven signet]] while using crystal equipment will provide a 10% chance to not consume charges.
In order to add charges to the crystal helm, [[crystal shard]]s must be used on it (this can be done before it is inactive as well), with each shard granting 100 charges, up to a maximum of 20,000. Dismantling a crystal helm will return the crystal armour seed to the player and doing so will lose all crystal shard charges that were previously loaded.
