{{External|rs}} {{otheruses|the crystal legs}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Active |version2 = Inactive |name1 = Crystal legs |name2 = Crystal legs (inactive) |image1 = [[File:Crystal legs.png]] |image2 = [[File:Crystal legs (inactive).png]] |release = [[25 July]] [[2019]] |update = Song of the Elves |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Wear, Check, Revert, Drop |options2 = Wear, Revert, Drop |wornoptions1 = Check |wornoptions2 = None |examine = A bright, shiny set of leg armour. |value = 1000000 |alchable = No |weight = 1.000 |id1 = 23979 |id2 = 23981 |leagueRegion = Tirannwn }} {{Synced switch |version1=[[File:Crystal legs detail.png|left|90px]] |version2=[[File:Crystal legs (inactive) detail.png|left|90px]]}} '''Crystal legs''' are a piece of [[crystal armour]] requiring 70 [[Defence]] and 50 [[Agility]] to equip. When equipped, a 5% damage bonus and 10% accuracy bonus is applied when using the [[crystal bow]] or [[Bow of Faerdhinen]]. This bonus stacks additively with the [[crystal body]] and [[crystal helmet]]'s bonuses, for a total of 15% damage and 30% accuracy. The bonus also stacks with the [[slayer helmet (i)]] and is useful for bosses similar to the [[Abyssal Sire]].
Players can create a pair of crystal legs via a [[singing bowl]] by combining 100 [[crystal shard]]s and two [[crystal armour seed]]s. Doing so requires level 72 [[Smithing]] and [[Crafting]] to [[crystal singing|sing]] the crystal (the levels can be [[Temporary skill boost|boosted]]), and grants 5,000 experience in both skills. Players can configure the charges while the legs are in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. If the player does not meet the Smithing and Crafting requirements, they can have [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for them for an extra 60 crystal shards, for a total of 160.
The legs' colours may also be changed to other colours of the [[Elven Clans]] by buying crystals from [[Lliann's Wares]] in [[Prifddinas]], which cost 500,000 coins each. It can also be reverted to its original colour by using the [[crystal of Meilyr]] on any variant of the legs.
If lost to another player in a dangerous PVP death, the crystal legs will revert to 2 crystal armour seeds, which will then be dropped for the killer. All crystal shards will be lost should this happen. If the crystal legs are protected on death, the legs will be kept, and will not lose any charges- similar to a blowpipe or trident.
When combined with an [[slayer helmet (i)|imbued slayer helmet]], the damage bonus from crystal armour pieces is multiplied by the 15% ranged damage boost from the helmet. Assuming players are wearing both the crystal body and legs, this results in a damage bonus of approximately 29.375%.
