==Trivia== *This is the only type of tea that cannot be used with a [[bucket of milk]] to make a milky version. *Nettle tea and POH tea have the empty option, but this standard tea does not. *In ''RuneScape Classic'', players were able to telegrab the display tea unlike in ''RuneScape 2''; it was tradeable. If the player dropped the display tea, they could not pick it up unless they used [[Telekinetic Grab]]. It was also used in scams occasionally. *[[Ghast]]s cannot rot tea. This may be because a cup of tea is classed as a potion. *Drinking a cup of tea does incur a combat delay similar to most healing items. *Players can give a cup of tea to [[Elsie]] on the second floor of the Varrock church. In exchange she will tell the player a story. * A variant [[Cup of tea (Zogre Flesh Eaters)|cup of tea]] can be found in [[Yanille]] and is involved in [[Zogre Flesh Eaters]].
