{{Infobox Item |name = Cupronickel bar |image = [[File:Cupronickel bar.png]] |release = [[19 November]] [[2025]] |update = Sailing is OUT TODAY! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Drop |examine = It's a bar of cupronickel. |value = 28 |weight = 1.814 |exchange = Yes |id = 32892 }} [[File:Cupronickel bar detail.png|130px|left]] A '''cupronickel bar''' is a metal bar used in [[shipbuilding]], as well as certain [[island amenities]]. It can be smelted using the [[Smithing]] skill at level 74 Smithing by using 2 [[copper ore]] and 1 [[nickel ore]] on a [[furnace]] or by using the [[Superheat Item]] spell from the standard spell book.
When attempting to make cupronickel bars at the [[Blast Furnace]], up to 14 nickel ore can be deposited at a time. As a result, players should deposit 18 copper ore and 9 nickel ore each run, withdrawing the bars once every three runs for a total of 27 bars per withdraw.
==Creation== <tabber> Standard= {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 74 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 42 |members = Yes |ticks = 5 |ticksnote = Make-X is 4, then 5. A single bar is 6. |facilities = Furnace |mat1 = Copper ore |mat1quantity = 2 |mat2 = Nickel ore |mat2quantity = 1 |output1 = Cupronickel bar |output1subtxt = Normal furnace }} |-| Blast Furnace= {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 74 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 42 |members = Yes |ticks = 11 |ticksnote = Multiple bars are completed at once |facilities = Blast Furnace |mat1 = Copper ore |mat1quantity = 2 |mat2 = Nickel ore |mat2quantity = 1 |output1 = Cupronickel bar |output1subtxt = Blast Furnace }} |-| Superheat= {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 74 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 42 |skill2 = Magic |skill2lvl = 43 |skill2boostable = Yes |skill2exp = 53 |members = Yes |ticks = 3 |mat1 = Copper ore |mat1quantity = 2 |mat2 = Nickel ore |mat2quantity = 1 |mat3 = Nature rune |mat4 = Fire rune |mat4quantity = 4 |output1 = Cupronickel bar |output1subtxt = Superheat }} </tabber>
==Products== {{Uses material list|Cupronickel bar}}
==Trivia== * In real life, {{wp|cupronickel}} is a copper-nickel alloy used in shipbuilding because of its resistance to corrosion. Unlike in ''Old School RuneScape'', this metal is usually silver in colour.
