{{Infobox Scenery |name = Curtain |image = [[File:Curtain (Basement of Doom).png|250x250px]] |release = [[7 April]] [[2016]] |update = Hell-Rats, Fairy Rings & Perks |members = Yes |quest = None |location = [[Basement of Doom]] |options = Enter |examine = It's covering a little alcove. |map = {{Map|x:3078,y:9899|x:3073,y:9882|x:3072,y:9896|x:3082,y:9878|plane=0|mapID=12|mtype=pin}} |id = 539 }} '''Curtains''' are found in the [[Evil Dave]]'s [[Basement of Doom]], and are used to access the [[Hell-Rat Behemoth]]s. A player can use their [[cat]] on the curtain, or attempt to enter it with their cat following them, in order to let their cat fight a behemoth. If the player attempts to enter the curtain themselves without a cat, they will be told that they are too big to enter the narrow alcove. Using a pet that isn't a hellcat on the curtain will open an interface with the message "Regrettably, that pet isn't sufficiently interested in killing rats.".
[[Bucket of milk|Buckets of milk]] or [[raw fish]] can be used on the curtain to heal the cat inside while it fights the Hell-rat Behemoths.
