{{HasTask|Custodian stalker}}
{{Redirect|Custodian|the NPC in Nardah|Shiratti the Custodian|the wiki user right|RuneScape:Custodians}}
[[File:Elder custodian stalker icon.png|left]]
'''Custodian stalkers''' are [[Slayer]] monsters found inside the [[Stalker Den]] that can be fought after the completion of the [[Shadows of Custodia]] [[quest]]. They can be assigned by [[Chaeldar]] and [[Nieve]]. There are [[multicombat]] areas where [[Dwarf multicannon|cannon]]s can be placed in the south-western side of the dungeon, and single-combat caverns in the south-eastern and northern parts.

The slayer stalkers all drop [[broken antler]]s, which are used to create [[Atlatl dart tips]] for creating [[atlatl dart]]s outside of subduing the [[Moons of Peril]]. The mature and elder variants are also able to drop the [[antler guard]], a powerful off-hand weapon boasting offensive stats in all styles, with no defence requirement to wield.

The book ''[[On Migration Patterns]]'' describes custodian stalkers as a sort of mutated rabbit with fangs, nocturnal apex predators that disrupted migration patterns upon establishing their presence in [[Custodia Pass]]. The stalkers are also known to have kidnapped several residents of [[Auburnvale]] and dragged them to the den; human corpses are scattered throughout it, apparently overtaken by the [[Strangler]]. However, despite being exposed to it, live humans are not infected, and coupled with the presence of skeletal remains, as well as a lack of infected humans or animals, suggests that it may be a different strain from the version that has overtaken [[The Stranglewood]].

