{{Infobox Item |name = Daeyalt essence |image = [[File:Daeyalt essence.png]] |release = [[4 June]] [[2020]] |update = Darkmeyer |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = Powerful essence made from daeyalt. |value = 20 |weight = 0.040 |id = 24704 }} [[File:Daeyalt essence detail.png|120px|left]] '''Daeyalt essence''' is an untradeable type of essence used in [[Runecraft]]. It is obtained in the [[daeyalt essence mine]] by trading [[daeyalt shard]]s with [[Noranna Tytanin]], who can be found near the exit in the north-east area of the mine. Each daeyalt shard trades for a single daeyalt essence, and all essence is sent directly to the player's [[bank]] (except in the case of [[Ironman Mode#Ultimate|UIMs]], who can only trade for as much essence as their [[inventory]] can currently hold).
[[Vyre noble clothing]] must be worn to trade in the shards for daeyalt essence. Mining the daeyalt shards requires level 60 [[Mining]] and completion of [[Sins of the Father]].
Daeyalt essence acts the same way as regular essence does, being able to be stored in [[essence pouch]]es. However, it gives 50% extra experience per essence. This bonus is multiplicative with the 70% bonus at the [[Ourania Altar]], for a total bonus of 155% extra experience. Above 90 Runecrafting one can expect to average roughly 23 experience per Daeyalt essence at the Ourania altar. Daeyalt essence '''cannot''' be used in place of [[dark essence fragments]] at the [[Kourend]]'s [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|Blood]] and [[Soul Altar]]s.
Using a mixture of daeyalt essence and [[pure essence]] in the same runecrafting trip will result in the daeyalt essence being used first and a second craft-runes action on the altar is required to then craft using the pure essence. Because of this, [[Achievement Diary]] tasks will fail unless you only use one type of essence.
==Products== {{Uses material list|Daeyalt essence}}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 29 May 2025 |update = Yama CAs & More! |change = [[Scarred extract]]s now work as expected with [[aether rune]]s when using daeyalt essence. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
{{Darkmeyer}} {{Runecraft}}

{{Infobox Location |name = Daeyalt essence mine |image = [[File:Daeyalt essence mine.png|300px]] |release = [[4 June]] [[2020]] |update = Darkmeyer |members = Yes |location = [[Darkmeyer]] |race = Vampyre juvinates, human slaves |map = {{Map|name=Daeyalt essence mine|x=3680|y=9757|mapID=10038|height=250}} |type = mine |leagueRegion = Morytania }} The '''daeyalt essence mine''' is a mine found beneath the city of [[Darkmeyer]], in the lower tier of the city just north-west of the [[Darkmeyer General Store]], indicated by a [[dungeon]] marker. The mine was once home to the [[Stone of Jas]], the presence of which caused the mineral deposits in the area to change, creating [[daeyalt essence]] and [[daeyalt ore]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Noranna Tytanin|quote=They say that an object of great power was once stored in this very cave. Apparently, the presence of this object created the daeyalt deposits.}}
The mine is closely associated with the [[Meiyerditch mine]].
==Transportation== {{Map|x=3632|y=3340|mtype=pin|align=left|caption=The essence mine's entrance}} The essence mine becomes available after completion of [[Sins of the Father]]. To reach the mine, several routes can be taken: * Using the Drakan's medallion [[Ver Sinhaza]] teleport, running to the nearest Vyrewatch (one is right on the west side of the bank) and asking to be sent to the mines, then asking the nearest Vampyre Juvinate to leave the mine while wearing the [[Vyre noble outfit]], and then running north and passing through the crack in the wall to enter Darkmeyer just south of the entrance. * Using a [[Hallowed crystal shard]] to teleport to the [[Hallowed Sepulchre]] lobby, and running south and then west from there. * Using the [[Drakan's medallion]] Darkmeyer teleport and running clockwise through the city until you reach the mine entrance in the lower tier of the city. This method takes ~60 seconds to reach the entrance after teleporting.
==Features== Mining the [[daeyalt shard]]s here requires level 60 [[Mining]] and completion of [[Sins of the Father]]. Within the mine, players will find three [[Daeyalt Essence (rock)|daeyalt essence rocks]], but only one is active at any given time, indicated by a brighter shade and a spiral of sparkles around it. The active rock changes randomly, roughly every 60 seconds, and players will need to run between them to continue mining. [[Daeyalt essence]] can be used in place of [[pure essence]] for [[runecraft]]ing, which will net players 50% more Runecraft experience for any given action.
Mining the essence gives stackable [[daeyalt shard]]s, which can be exchanged for [[daeyalt essence]] via [[Noranna Tytanin]] on the eastern side of the mine for an equal amount. The essence will be sent directly to the player's bank. However, players will need to wear [[vyre noble clothing]] to interact with Noranna.
While mining essence, players receive 2–3 shards and 5 experience for every roll. With a [[dragon pickaxe|dragon]] or [[crystal pickaxe]], players can obtain approximately 4,000 [[daeyalt shard]]s and 8851 Mining experience per hour. Unlike at the [[dense essence mine]], the crystal pickaxe increases the rates of the mined essence and thus consumes charges.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1269236600409645057|date=6 June 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107301|archivedate=6 July 2020|quote=The difference is that it does help with the rate slightly at the daeyalt essence, whereas it does not help at all in Zeah. So it takes charges in one place but not the other.}} [[Tick manipulation]] may be used to mine essence, particularly 1.5-tick methods to obtain shards nearly twice as quickly (for up to 9,000 per hour). [[Mining enhancers]] (e.g. Varrock armour) '''do not''' increase the amount of shards received, though the experience boosting effect of [[prospector kit]] works normally. Players are also able to receive [[uncut gems]] while mining daeyalt essence, so it may be worthwhile to bring a [[gem bag]] for extended trips; a charged [[amulet of glory]] may also be used to increase the rate of gems mined, although this lowers the rate of obtaining shards.
There are also 13 [[daeyalt rocks]] found here, and a steel pickaxe spawn by the northern essence.
==Inhabitants== *[[Noranna Tytanin]] *[[Slave (daeyalt essence mine)|Slaves]] *[[Vampyre Juvinate (Daeyalt essence mine)|Vampyre Juvinates]]
