==Strategy==
[[Protection prayers]], [[Bones to Peaches]], [[Guthan the Infested's equipment|Guthan's]], and the [[Saradomin godsword]] [[special attack]] are all viable means of surviving for extended periods. Players with 70 [[Prayer]] can use a [[dragonbone necklace]] and [[bonecrusher]]/[[bonecrusher necklace]] to sustain more Prayer points.

The dagannoths in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]] can be [[safespot]]ted, but only with difficulty. For safespot 1, dagannoths must be lured to the side to prevent them pathing to the player. If using melee, this area can also be used to control the number of dagannoths that can attack you at once.

Safespot 2 uses a [[Warped Jelly]] as a safespot, as they are not [[Aggressiveness|aggressive]]. This safespot works best when the dagannoths are still aggressive, as they will line up in front of the jelly, allowing for easy kills.

<gallery>
File:Dagannoth (Catacombs of Kourend, 1) safespot.png|Safespot 1, trapping dagannoths around the corner
File:Dagannoth (Catacombs of Kourend, 2) safespot.png|Using safespot 1 such that only one dagannoth can attack at once
File:Dagannoth (Catacombs of Kourend, 3) safespot.png|Safespot 2, using a [[Warped Jelly]] to create a safespot
</gallery>

When killing the dagannoths in the Lighthouse, players can sell noted food to [[Jossik]] in the Lighthouse and buy it back in unnoted form for a small amount of money.

The dagannoths in [[Jormungand's Prison]] only attack with melee, are in multi-combat, and a cannon can be set. No food is required here if using [[Protect from Melee|Protect from Melee.]]

