{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Dagannoth bones |image = [[File:Dagannoth bones.png]] |release = [[7 November]] [[2005]] |update = Waterbirth Island - deeper, darker, deadlier! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Bury, Drop |examine = These would feed a dogfish for months! |value = 150 |weight = 1.500 |exchange = Yes |id = 6729 }} [[File:Dagannoth bones detail.png|left|150px]] '''Dagannoth bones''' are bones dropped by [[Dagannoth Rex]], [[Dagannoth Prime]], and [[Dagannoth Supreme]]. They are not obtained as drops from regular [[Dagannoth]], who only drop standard [[bones]].
Dagannoth bones give 125 [[Prayer]] experience when buried. This can be increased by offering the bones in different ways: * 375 XP when casting [[Sinister Offering]]. * 375 XP when offered at the [[sacred bone burner]] after the appropriate faith level has been achieved. * 437.5 XP when offered at a [[gilded altar]] with two burners lit. * 500 XP when offered at the [[Ectofuntus]] in the form of [[dagannoth bonemeal]]. * 500 XP when [[Dagannoth bones (blessed)|blessed]] and broken down into [[blessed bone shards]] and offered at the [[libation bowl]], or 600 XP when offered with a [[jug of blessed sunfire wine]]. [[Virilis]] outside the altar will exchange noted bones for 10 coins each. * 875 XP on average when offered at the [[Chaos Temple (hut)|Chaos Temple]] in the Wilderness. Each offering gives 437.5 XP, which is the same as the gilded altars with two burners lit, but with an additional 50% chance to not consume the bones.
Dagannoth bones cannot be turned into [[Peach|peaches]] via the [[Bones to Peaches]] spell.
If players have completed the [[elite Fremennik Diary]], the bones will be dropped as [[bank note]]s. This can be turned off by talking to [[Thorodin]].
