{{Infobox Weapon Group
|name = Dagger
|images = {{plinkp|Bronze dagger}}{{plinkp|Iron dagger}}{{plinkp|Steel dagger}}{{plinkp|Black dagger}}{{plinkp|White dagger}}{{plinkp|Mithril dagger}}{{plinkp|Adamant dagger}}{{plinkp|Rune dagger}}{{plinkp|Dragon dagger}}
|primary = [[Stab]]
|secondary = [[Slash]]
|speed = 4
}}

'''Daggers''' are generally small, fast [[melee]] [[weapons]]. Most daggers are [[Weapons/Categories#stab sword|stab swords]] which primarily use [[Stab weapons|stab]] attack styles but also have an option for a [[slash]]ing style; though there are many items thought of as daggers that either belong to different [[Weapons/Categories|weapon categories]] or aren't even wieldable.

Interestingly, despite presenting as melee-only weapons, many daggers have a positive magic attack bonus.

[[Members]] have an advantage with daggers in that many can be [[poison]]ed. They can be tipped with [[weapon poison]], [[weapon poison+]], or [[weapon poison++]], though they can not be poisoned with [[karambwan paste]].

[[Scimitar]]s and [[sword]]s are generally stronger than daggers of their tier, and also attack at the same speed. Therefore they are preferred more by most players, especially when weapon poison does not matter. 

The daggers that see the most use are often the [[dragon dagger|dragon]] and [[abyssal dagger]]s due to their highly damaging and accurate [[special attacks]], for damaging monsters or securing kills in [[PvP]] combat; and the [[bone dagger]] for its defence-reducing special attack against certain [[bosses]]. There are alternatives that often (but not always) outclass these special attacks, but usually at a much higher cost.

==Standard daggers==
Every dagger in the standard [[metal]] hierarchy can be poisoned.
