==Possible rewards==
{{Skill info
|skill1name = Smithing
|skill1lvl = 1
|skill1exp = 25
|facility = [[Armour stand]]
}}

There is a chance of breaking the damaged armour and receiving nothing. The success rate is higher with a higher Smithing level.

{{DropLogProject|jagex=yes|success=yes}}
{{Skilling success chart|label=Damaged armour repair chance|xlabel=Smithing level
|label1=Damaged armour|low1=75|high1=240|color1=olive|image1=Damaged armour.png
}}

{{DropLogProject|jagex=yes|type=repairs}}
{{DropsTableHead}}
{{DropsLineSkill|name=Iron platebody|quantity=1|rarity=57/100|skill=smithing}}
{{DropsLineSkill|name=Bronze platebody|quantity=1|rarity=24/100|skill=smithing}}
{{DropsLineSkill|name=Steel platebody|quantity=1|rarity=10/100|skill=smithing}}
{{DropsLineSkill|name=Black platebody|quantity=1|rarity=5/100|skill=smithing}}
{{DropsLineSkill|name=Mithril platebody|quantity=1|rarity=4/100|skill=smithing}}
{{DropsTableBottom}}

Considering the [[Grand Exchange]] values and probabilities of obtaining each platebody, repairing damaged armour will on average yield {{Coins|floor (0.57*{{GEP|Iron platebody}} + 0.24*{{GEP|Bronze platebody}} + 0.05*{{GEP|Black platebody}} + 0.10*{{GEP|Steel platebody}} + 0.04*{{GEP|Mithril platebody}}) }}. Thus repairing damaged armour is hardly worth it even in bulk.

