{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Location |name = Dareeyak |image = [[File:Ruins (west).png|300px]] |release = [[13 August]] [[2001]] |update = Wilderness system online |aka = Ruins (west) |members = No |location = [[Wilderness]] |wilderness = 21-24 |teleport = [[Dareeyak Teleport]] |music = [[Troubled]] |map = {{Map|name=Dareeyak|x=2970|y=3695|height=250|zoom=2}} |leagueRegion = Wilderness }} '''Dareeyak''' was a [[Zaros]]ian settlement that was located in what is now the [[Wilderness]]. It was considered a low priority target for enemy forces{{CiteNPC|npc=Golem (Desert Treasure II)|quote=Dareeyak is a low priority target for enemy forces. Consider taking advantage of this.}} during the [[God Wars]] in the [[Third Age]], but it was ultimately destroyed.
The [[Ruins (west)|western ruins]] in level 23 [[Wilderness]] are all that remains of Dareeyak today, and they remain the destination of the [[Dareeyak Teleport]] [[Ancient Magicks]] spell. It is unclear if the nearby [[Bandit Camp (Wilderness)|stronghold]] currently inhabited by bandits were considered part of Dareeyak.
==References== {{Reflist}}
[[Category:Lore]] [[Category:Wilderness]] {{Zarosian Empire}}

{{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Teak |version2 = Mahogany |version3 = Marble |version4 = Raging Echoes |name = Dareeyak Portal |image1 = [[File:Dareeyak Portal (teak).png|250x250px]] |image2 = [[File:Dareeyak Portal (mahogany).png|250x250px]] |image3 = [[File:Dareeyak Portal (marble).png|250x250px]] |image4 = [[File:Dareeyak Portal (Raging Echoes).png|250x250px]] |release = [[25 February]] [[2026]] |update = Cow Boss is Out Today! |members = Yes |location = [[Portal Chamber]] |options = Enter, Remove |examine = A gateway to Dareeyak. |map = No |id1 = 60793 |id2 = 60803 |id3 = 60813 |id4 = 60777 }} A '''Dareeyak Portal''' can be built in the [[portal chamber]] of a [[player-owned house]]. It will teleport players to the [[Ruins (west)|ruins]] south of [[The Forgotten Cemetery]] in level 23 [[Wilderness]]. Because it teleports players into the Wilderness, it will pop-up a warning prompt to confirm if the player wishes to teleport.
Players must first build a portal frame, then use the centrepiece to direct the portal. This requires level 78 [[Magic]] and completion of [[Desert Treasure I]]. The cost to direct the portal is 200 [[air rune]]s, 300 [[fire rune]]s and 200 [[law rune]]s.
==Destination== {{Map|2968,3696|mtype=square|r=2|align=left}}{{clear|left}}
==Comparison== Portals use 100 times the runes of the base spell, whereas individual additions to the [[portal nexus]] use 1,000 times the amount. {| class="wikitable defaultcenter" !colspan=2| Teleport ! !colspan=2| Portal chamber ! !colspan=2| Portal nexus |- |{{plinkt|Air rune}} x 2 ! |{{plinkt|Air rune}} x 200 ! |{{plinkt|Air rune}} x 2,000 |- |{{plinkt|Fire rune}} x 3 ! |{{plinkt|Fire rune}} x 300 ! |{{plinkt|Fire rune}} x 3,000 |- |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 2 ! |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 200 ! |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 2,000 |}
{{Portal chamber}}

{{External|rs}} {{otheruses|the teleport spell|the teleport tablet|Dareeyak teleport (tablet)}} {{Infobox Spell |name = Dareeyak Teleport |image = [[File:Dareeyak Teleport.png]] |release = [[18 April]] [[2005]] |update = Desert Treasure |members = Yes |level = 78 |spellbook = Ancient |type = Teleport |exp = 88 |cost = {{RuneReq|Law=2|Fire=3|Air=2}} |speed = 5 ticks |description = A teleportation spell |anim = [[File:Ancient teleport.gif]] |sound = [[File:Teleport (Ancient Magicks).ogg]] }} [[File:Dareeyak Teleport icon (mobile).png|left|class=pageimage]] '''Dareeyak Teleport''' is a spell in the [[Ancient Magicks]] spellbook, requiring a [[Magic]] level of 78 to cast. It teleports the caster to the [[Ruins (west)|ruins]] south of [[The Forgotten Cemetery]] in level 23 [[Wilderness]]. It can be useful for easy access to the [[Crazy archaeologist]].
As with all Ancient Magicks spells, the quest [[Desert Treasure I]] must be completed to cast this spell.
