{{External|rs}} {{Otheruses|def=no}} {{Infobox Music |name = Dark |number = 32 |file = [[File:Dark.ogg]] |release = [[15 March]] [[2004]] |update = RS2 Music player and fixes |members = No |location = [[Wilderness]] |hint = This track unlocks in the Wilderness. |quest = No |instruments = Tubular Bells, Pizzicato Strings, Orchestral Harp, String Ensemble 1, String Ensemble 2, Choir Aahs, French Horn, Synth Brass 1, Pan Flute, Custom Percussion |duration = 02:52 |album = ''[[RuneScape: Original Soundtrack Classics]]'' |composer = Ian Taylor |map = {{Map:Wilderness music|height=150|zoom=-2}} {{Map:Wilderness 2 music|height=150|zoom=1}} |cacheid = 326 |sortname = Dark |unlockdetail = Unlocked in the [[Wilderness]]. |tempo=115 BPM|signature=4/4}} '''Dark''' is a [[music]] track that is unlocked in the [[Wilderness]] and plays in the [[Wilderness Agility Course Dungeon]].
In Classic mode, the track plays north-east of the [[Chaos Temple (Wilderness)|Wilderness Chaos Temple]].
{{Map|3264,3648|3264,3712|3392,3712|3392,3648|plane=0|mapID=0|mtype=polygon|bucket=hist|caption=Location before 2021 and on Classic mode|align=left}}
==Analysis== The track is notable as it features four different short sections threaded together, with none of them repeated. The opening section lasts exactly fifty seconds, and features French horn along to a haunting background sound with a thumping drum beat underneath it, and this segues into a short chorus solo. The second section opens with a short piano solo. It is livelier and retains the chorus from the first section, which plays amongst a quick synthesised melody; this lasts just under forty seconds. The third section uses the same French horn from the opening and the same haunting background sound, but this time plays a slower, more woeful melody instead that lasts around thirty seconds. Once this dies down, the final section begins, which includes drums, bells, light piano, flutes and synthesised strings working together to create a moderately-paced, mysterious melody that lasts just over fifty seconds in total. Just as the section closes and track fades to nothing, the chime of a bell marks the finish.
==Versions== {| class="wikitable embed-audio-links" |- !Version !Release !Music Track |- |1 |[[1 June]] [[2004]] |[[File:Dark (v1).ogg]] |- |2 |[[6 March]] [[2007]] |[[File:Dark.ogg]] |}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 26 May 2021 |update = Clans Full Launch |change = On newly released Classic music mode, Dark has been set to play at its pre-shuffling-update location. }} {{Subject changes |date = 28 April 2021 |update = Arceuus Spellbook Beta and A Kingdom Divided Preparation |change = Dark has been made part of Wilderness music genre. }} {{Subject changes |date = 1 March 2018 |update = QoL Improvements & Deadman Permadeath Beta |change = Added unlock hint for this track: 'This track unlocks in the Wilderness.' }} {{Subject changes |date = 26 October 2004 |update = Treasure Trails and Changes |change = Dark has been replaced with [[Barbarianism]] in [[Barbarian Village]] and [[Edgeville Dungeon]]. }} {{Subject changes |date = 18 October 2004 |update = Mortton Shades and Mage Armour |change = The track was renamed from 'Dark2' to 'Dark'. }} {{Subject changes |date = 15 March 2004 |update = RS2 Music player and fixes |change = Added to game as 'Dark2' and set to play north-east of Wilderness Chaos Temple, in Barbarian Village and southern part of Edgeville Dungeon. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
==Trivia== *The music track [[Intrepid]] features a remix of the third and fourth section of this song, except the miniature beats are not included.
