{{Transcript|scenery}}

==When a player is the first to discover a crashed star==
* {{Tbox|Congratulations! You were the first person to find this star! Your star dust gain will be doubled for the next 300 dust you mine!}}
* {{tact|end}}

==Prospecting the crashed star==
* {{tbox|This is a size-[9/8/7/6/5/4/3/2/1] star. A Mining level of at least [90/80/70/60/50/40/30/20/10] is required to mine this layer. It has been mined [#]% of the way to the next layer.}}
* {{tact|end}}

==Mining the crashed star==
* {{tcond|If the player does not have a pickaxe or does not have the required [[Mining]] level for the pickaxe:}}
** {{tbox|You need a pickaxe to mine this star. You do not have a pickaxe which you have the Mining level to use.}}
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player meets the requirements for their pickaxe but does not have the required Mining level for the star:}}
** {{tbox|You need a Mining level of [#] to mine this star.}}
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player has a pickaxe with the requirement to mine the star:}}
** {{mes|You swing your pick at the star.}}
* {{tcond|If the player has a discovery bonus whilst mining the star:}}
** {{mes|Your star discovery bonus will grant you another [250, 200, 150, 100, 50] star dust before it runs out.}}
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player uses up all of their star discovery bonus whilst mining the star:}}
** {{mes|colour=#ff0000|Your star discovery bonus has been used up.}}
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player finds a clue geode:}}
** {{mes|You find a clue geode!}}
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the star disappears:}}
** {{mes|The star disintegrates into dust.}}
** {{tact|end}}

